INT. DRIVE-THROUGH WEDDING CHAPEL - NIGHT

Pink neon. A window hatch cut into a stucco wall. An organ plays on a loop from a speaker on a post. A plastic arch of roses.

Inside the booth: REVEREND-ISH LEONARD "LENNY" ABIODUN, 50s, in a rented robe, drinks from a paper cup.

A car pulls up. Headlights wash the arch. Out of the driver's window leans BIANCA STROZZI-OKORO, 30s, in a white dress and a leather jacket. In the passenger seat sits ELIAS NAKAMURA-FLORES, 30s, bow tie crooked.

LENNY
Welcome to the Chapel of Quick Vows. What's your order?

BIANCA
Two vows, no fries.

ELIAS
We'd like the premium.

LENNY
The premium has a rose.

ELIAS
Then give us the rose.

BIANCA
Elias, we don't have time.

ELIAS
Bianca, the rose is five dollars.

LENNY
It's a real rose.

BIANCA
It's plastic.

LENNY
It's a real plastic rose.

ELIAS
We'll take the rose.

Bianca sighs. Hands cash. Lenny passes a rose through the window. Elias holds it. She snatches it. They both laugh.

LENNY
Names?

BIANCA
Bianca Strozzi-Okoro.

ELIAS
Elias Nakamura-Flores.

LENNY
Do you, Elias, take this woman...

ELIAS
I do.

LENNY
I haven't finished.

BIANCA
He knows the rest.

LENNY
Do you, Bianca...

BIANCA
Absolutely.

LENNY
By the power vested in me by the state of Nevada and a two-day online course...

ELIAS
Lenny.

LENNY
...I pronounce you...

BIANCA
Lenny!

LENNY
...married.

Silence. The organ stutters. Elias leans out and kisses Bianca. She grabs his lapel. The horn honks, long and joyful.

LENNY (CONT'D)
That's twelve dollars, plus tip.

BIANCA
We have to talk about the license.

ELIAS
What about the license?

BIANCA
I forgot to buy it.

Lenny drops his cup.
